Personally, I don't worry so much about HPs.  The ONLY thing in the
endgame you have to worry about are the air elementals.  Sufficient
wands of teleportation and death, or a small stash of potions of full
healing will help you through that level.  Don't let Death hit you on
astral either, but that's not too hard with sufficiently good ranged
attacks.  My ranger I ascended over the weekend took out the riders
with 4 blessed +6 arrows with the +0 Longbow of Diana (Famine thrice,
Pestilence twice, Death once).

Since I had a HD crash, I've had 5 ascensions on 3.4.3:

Class       HP  [max]
Valk        197 [199]
Valk        130 [158]
Ran         202 [202]
Arc         187 [240]
Cav         163 [174]

I lost the record of my monk, who ascended weaponless with about 130
HP (Death knocked him down from around 160).  The Ran only got above
200 when Pestilence sickened him and the unicorn horn failed the first
time.  After the second round, I felt much worse, so I decided to go
with the 100% cure.  The potion was blessed, and took me from 194 to
202 HPs.  I probably should have let Death touch me once to drop back
below 200!

As others have mentioned, timely prayers at altars will also boost HPs
(you are surrounded by a golden glow).

